From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: s3k000 <144541403+s3k000@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:16:20 -0800
Subject: hw/display: add pvg-fwd, which forwards apple-gfx-pci to another
 process

pvg-fwd shows the guest the PCI function apple-gfx-pci shows, with the
same IDs and BARs, but holds no device of its own. Register reads and
writes go over a socket to the process that has the device, and the
interrupts it raises come back the same way. That process reads and
writes the guest's memory itself: it is handed the file behind each
range of RAM over the socket, so the machine's RAM has to be a shared
memory backend.

  -object memory-backend-shm,id=ram,size=4G -M virt,memory-backend=ram
  -device pvg-fwd,socket=/path/to/the/process/s/socket

On a macOS host the other process is Guesthouse's graphics process,
guesthouse-pvg-host, which keeps the framework's device behind a guard.
